
## Alternative: Simplified Version with Pure PHP Library

If you prefer an even simpler approach without complex dependencies, here's a minimalist version using the `phpqrcode` library:

**simple-qr-generator.php**
```php
<?php
/**
 * Simple QR Code Generator using phpqrcode library
 */

// Include the phpqrcode library
require_once 'phpqrcode/qrlib.php';

// Create output directory
if (!file_exists('qrcodes')) {
    mkdir('qrcodes', 0755);
}

// Process form submission
if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST') {
    $text = $_POST['text'] ?? '';
    $size = $_POST['size'] ?? 10;
    $margin = $_POST['margin'] ?? 1;
    
    if (!empty($text)) {
        // Generate unique filename
        $filename = 'qrcodes/qr-' . md5($text . time()) . '.png';
        
        // Generate QR code
        QRcode::png($text, $filename, QR_ECLEVEL_L, $size, $margin);
        
        // Display result
        echo '<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>QR Code Generated</title></head><body>';
        echo '<h1>QR Code Generated!</h1>';
        echo '<img src="' . $filename . '" alt="QR Code">';
        echo '<p><a href="' . $filename . '" download>Download QR Code</a></p>';
        echo '<p><a href="simple-qr-generator.php">Generate Another</a></p>';
        echo '</body></html>';
        exit;
    }
}
?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Simple QR Code Generator</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Simple QR Code Generator</h1>
    <form method="POST">
        <textarea name="text" rows="4" cols="50" placeholder="Enter text or URL"></textarea><br>
        <label>Size: <input type="number" name="size" value="10" min="1" max="20"></label><br>
        <label>Margin: <input type="number" name="margin" value="1" min="0" max="10"></label><br>
        <button type="submit">Generate QR Code</button>
    </form>
</body>
</html>